# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""/procedimientos/rinoplastia — Spanish copy.

Three statements, and the third is the one no practice publishes.

  "La nariz que ve a los tres meses no es la que se queda."
  The slowest result on the site. Anyone showing a two-week reveal is showing
  swelling. Keep it flat and keep the timeline numbers exactly as sourced.

  "Su piel decide cuán definido puede ser el resultado."
  Not something surgery changes, and raising it after operating is too late.

  "Aproximadamente una de cada diez va a querer una revisión."
  Published revision rates for primary rhinoplasty run about five to fifteen
  per cent — higher than anything else on this site, and the page says so with
  its own number. That paragraph is the most easily deleted thing here and the
  most valuable. It is not an admission of poor surgery; it is what operating on
  millimetres of cartilage costs, and a patient who reads it before booking is
  the patient who does not feel deceived afterwards.

Terms: "columela", "tabique" (with "septum" where the compound "septoplastia"
carries it), "válvula interna". "Rinoplastia" and "septorrinoplastia" are the
names patients search.
"""

H1 = ["Rinoplastia"]

